Subject: [PATCH 0036] intra: only prepare the second MRL reference line when it is read

av2_build_intra_predictors_high() maintains two independent neighbour
reference lines:

    above_row_1st / left_col_1st   the ordinary reference line
    above_row_2nd / left_col_2nd   the second line, for multi-line MRL

The _2nd pair is consumed at exactly two call sites, both inside the
directional-mode branch, and both guarded by the same predicate:

    xd->mi[0]->multi_line_mrl && mrl_index && (tx_size != TX_4X4)

Everything that produces the _2nd buffers, however, runs unconditionally:

  * two avm_memset16() calls of NUM_INTRA_NEIGHBOUR_PIXELS (192 uint16 =
    384 bytes) each, at the top of the function;
  * the left-column copy loops and their edge-extension memset16;
  * the above-row memcpy of n_top_px (plus n_topright_px) and its
    edge-extension memset16;
  * the above-left corner writes.

mrl_index is 0 for the large majority of blocks, so in the common case all
of that is written and never read.

This patch hoists the predicate to the top of the function as
need_2nd_line and guards every _2nd producer with it. The two consumers are
rewritten to test need_2nd_line rather than re-deriving the predicate, so
the "written iff read" invariant is syntactically enforced rather than
maintained by hand in two places.

WHY THIS IS BIT-EXACT

It removes writes to buffers that are provably never read on the paths
where the writes are skipped. The predicate at the producers is the same
expression, on the same variables, as the predicate at the consumers --
mbmi is xd->mi[0], and mrl_index and tx_size are function parameters, none
of which change between the two points. No value that reaches the
bitstream is computed differently.

Note the _2nd buffers are function-local DECLARE_ALIGNED stack arrays, so
skipping the memset cannot leak state across calls into anything that is
read: the only readers are the two guarded call sites.

SIZE OF THE EFFECT

From a callgrind profile of the current tip (320x192, 3 frames, 1 thread),
avm_memset16 reached through av2_build_intra_predictors_high is

    cpu-used=5   1.00% of retired instructions
    cpu-used=2   0.81% of retired instructions

Half of that is the two unconditional _2nd memsets, and the _2nd copy
loops and memcpy add more on top -- they land in the 0.62%-0.76% self cost
of av2_build_intra_predictors_high and in the memcpy lines.

MEASURED

Retired instructions under callgrind, same clip and settings:

    unpatched   176,252,929,353
    patched     175,514,192,652
    removed         738,736,701   =  0.42%

This is the smallest of the three memory-traffic patches in this round
(0034 is 2.67%, 0037 is 4.24%), and it is worth being clear that 0.42% is
not much. It is included because it is bit-exact and because the argument
is a clean locality property rather than a judgement call -- so it costs
nothing to carry and cannot fail the ratio bar at any preset. If only one
of the three is worth a CTC slot, it is not this one.

MEASURING IT

Use retired-instruction counts under callgrind, not wall clock. The local
wall-clock noise floor is several percent and has repeatedly produced
sign-disagreeing reps on changes of this size -- a 0.42% change is roughly
an order of magnitude below what wall clock can resolve here. The work
removed is memory traffic, so instruction counts understate the real
saving.

VERIFICATION

Bit-exactness was checked by comparing .obu md5 against the unpatched
build across clip x preset x qindex, including low-speed presets where MRL
is actually exercised (the path on which the _2nd buffers ARE read, so the
guard must let the work through).

